Task: Fix issue #1028 where benign concurrent cache saves trigger warning annotations in GitHub Actions.

Problem Description:
In `dist/save-cache/index.cjs`, bundled `ReserveCacheError` class is renamed by the bundler into `class _ReserveCacheError`, causing `typedError.name === ReserveCacheError.name` to evaluate to false (comparing 'ReserveCacheError' with '_ReserveCacheError').
Consequently, benign concurrent cache collisions are logged as warning annotations rather than info messages.

Requirements:
1. Run `node reproduce_issue.js` to observe the failure.
2. Fix the bundler configuration in `scripts/build-dist.mjs` (or error handling) so that error class names are preserved in the bundle (e.g. using keepNames: true in esbuild).
3. Re-build the bundle using `node scripts/build-dist.mjs`.
4. Run `node reproduce_issue.js` to verify that class name matches instance name.
5. Run `npm run test:unit` to verify that existing unit tests pass.

